    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters July 25 with a clear hierarchy of efficiency, led by **James Wood** (75.97) and **Brice Turang** (72.70). **James Wood** presents the highest ceiling on the board today, benefiting from a soft matchup against Bratt (5.90 xERA) and an elite xwOBA profile that overcomes the minor friction of a tough hold pitcher. Meanwhile, **Brice Turang** is our anchor for category scarcity; he enjoys a massive 19% SP skill boost against Feltner, making him an essential start to secure speed and contact metrics. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) and **Austin Riley** (72.42) round out our top-tier plays, with **Austin Riley** capitalizing on a massive 16% park factor adjustment that pushes his scoring well above his baseline. \n\nOur most difficult roster decision was leaving **Isaac Paredes** (52.31) on the bench. While his dynamic platoon edge and batting order placement provided a solid foundation, he ultimately fell short of the threshold required to displace starters like **Josh Naylor** (52.93) or **Gabriel Moreno** (51.75). The optimizer prioritized the SP matchups and volume of the current starters, leaving **Isaac Paredes** as the primary pivot should any late-inning injury news emerge. We are also monitoring the risks associated with **Seiya Suzuki** (45.36) and **Jose Caballero** (51.18); both face significant headwinds due to elite opposing pitch velocity and high-efficiency catchers, which threaten to stifle our stolen base opportunities despite their respective order advantages. \n\nWith **Corbin Carroll** (65.34) continuing to weaponize his sprint speed despite a tough draw against Griffin, we are banking on his ability to manufacture runs on the basepaths where others might struggle against high-caliber pitching. We have opted to keep depth pieces like **Dalton Rushing** (38.41), **Edwin Arroyo** (44.91), and **Cole Young** (40.15) benched today, as their projections fail to clear the efficiency bar set by our daily specialists. As the day unfolds, look for **Corbin Carroll** and **Brice Turang** to be the primary drivers of our 5x5 output, provided our lineup navigates the risks posed by the high-skill arms of Griffin and Skenes.",
